  "counter_interpretation": [
    "Registration and frame bytes are cumulative structural charges, not peak heap.",
    "Whole-table waits count encounters, not elapsed waiting or idle-core percentage.",
    "The work reports are separate validation executions; their nanosecond counters are not timing-lane medians.",
    "New root read/hit/job counters were absent in earlier code; the corresponding path did not exist.",
    "Neither sum-bits variant enters the new background shared-root path.",
    "Empty event polls already have an atomic readiness fast path; their count alone does not establish lock contention.",
    "The worker owns the sole mutating index, with short source read/worker write locks. This is not independent concurrent mutation of all graph state.",
    "Lookup guard order, index sharing and source overlap changed together; their individual effects are not isolated."
